# Paper-trading state is COMMITTED on purpose during Phase 2.
#
# The book is simulated — virtual Rs.10,00,000, no broker account behind it —
# so publishing it exposes nothing real, and putting the ledger in git history
# makes the forward out-of-sample record timestamped and tamper-evident. That
# record is the only clean out-of-sample left after the 24-month holdout was
# observed, so it is worth more in the repo than out of it.
#
# >>> RESTORE THESE BEFORE PHASE 3. <<<
# The moment real orders are placed, positions.json holds actual holdings and
# share counts and orders_*.csv holds actual order sizes, on a PUBLIC repo:
#   live/positions.json
#   live/orders_*.csv
#   live/paper_ledger.csv
#
# dashboard.html stays ignored either way — it is generated output, fully
# rebuildable from the two files above, and would churn on every render.
live/dashboard.html
